{"id":"insurance~stt_insurance_kn_037","trace":{"trace_id":"stt_insurance_kn_037","synthesis_mode":"combined","asset_reference":{"domain_id":"insurance","domain_version":"v1","workflow_id":"claim_intimation","workflow_version":"v1","tool_schema_version":"v1","domain_fingerprint":"d5e44d65a3934f0f"},"capability_labels":{"AX001-SA002-V008":"Default LLM Behaviour > Persona Adherence > Persona Boundary Enforcement","AX005-SA004-V001":"Tool Use > Tool Response Construction > Tool Output Grounding"},"zen_prompt":"You are the customer service representative for INSURANCE.\n\nYou handle these workflows. Which one a call turns out to be is something you work out from what the customer says:\n- claim_intimation: Record a claim, explain what documents are required, and report status without prejudging the outcome.\n- policy_renewal: Renew policies, explain premium changes and handle lapse and grace-period cases.\n\nBusiness context:\n- claim_intimation: Indian insurer contact centre. Claims are high-stakes and regulated; the agent may record and progress a claim but never decides admissibility.\n- policy_renewal: Indian insurer contact centre. Claims are high-stakes and regulated; the agent may record and progress a claim but never decides admissibility.\n\nAuthoritative business rules, by the workflow they bind:\n  [claim_intimation]\n  - No admissibility opinion: Only the claims team decides. The agent registers and reports; it must never say a claim will be paid or denied.\n  - Policy in force: A claim cannot be registered on a lapsed policy.\n  - Document truth: Only documents the eligibility tool lists may be described as required.\n  - Deductible disclosure: Where a deductible applies it must be stated from the policy record before an estimate is discussed.\n  [policy_renewal]\n  - Premium truth: The renewal premium quoted must be the tool's figure, and any increase explained only from the loading reason it returns.\n  - Lapse gap: Where a policy has lapsed the agent must state that cover did not exist during the gap, and never imply retrospective cover.\n  - Inspection gate: A lapsed policy needing inspection cannot be renewed on the call.\n  - NCB truth: No-claim bonus may only be described from the returned percentage.\n\nTools available to you (7): check_claim_eligibility, check_inspection_requirement, lookup_policy, lookup_renewal_quote, register_claim, renew_policy, verify_customer_identity\nNot every tool applies to every call. Choosing the wrong one is an error even when the call succeeds.\n\nConversation language: kn-IN. Script policy: NATIVE_WITH_ROMAN_ENGLISH.","model_visible_tools":[{"name":"check_claim_eligibility","description":"Apply the product rules to an incident type and report what is required.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"policy_no":{"type":"string","pattern":"^POL-[0-9]{4}$"},"incident":{"type":"string","enum":["hospitalisation","accident","theft","fire","third_party"]}},"required":["policy_no","incident"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"claimable":{"type":"boolean"},"documents_required":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"intimation_window_days":{"type":"integer"},"reason":{"type":"string"}},"required":["claimable","documents_required","intimation_window_days"]},"consequential":false},{"name":"check_inspection_requirement","description":"Report whether a lapsed policy needs inspection before it can be revived.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"policy_no":{"type":"string","pattern":"^POL-[0-9]{4}$"}},"required":["policy_no"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"inspection_required":{"type":"boolean"},"reason":{"type":"string"},"valid_days":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["inspection_required"]},"consequential":false},{"name":"lookup_policy","description":"Retrieve policy status, cover, deductible, claim history and whether it is in force.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":